A||||6||Gokart||Sinking door!
Z||000000||Gokart||05-30-99||07:23 PM||||Today I almost s... when I couldn't get out of my car because the top of the door window was catching the plexiglass sail window! I discovered it was because I could literally lift my drivers side door about 2 inches. After looking it over I don't know what can be done because the pin in the hinge is in place, and looks fine. I think the years of use made the hole that the pin is in too big!? Problem is that piece is actually welded to the door for uneasy replacement. Any suggesstions before my door is rubbing on the street? TIA
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||05-30-99||07:33 PM||||I had the same problem. The top hinge pin worked it's way up,Not out,but up. I knocked it back in with a hammer. Hope thats it.
Z||000002||theogre||05-30-99||08:33 PM||||replace both hinge pins in that door. thay are in the red "help" packaging at most parts stores. about 10$ for pins and bushings.
Z||000003||Gokart||05-31-99||04:41 AM||||I was hoping it was going to be as easy as knocking a pin back down, but the pin is in place and looks fine. Its the hole that the pin sits in, I think its gotten too large from years of use. Maybe the bushings in help packaging at the parts store will do? TIA
Z||000004||Carrolles||06-01-99||09:53 AM||||The Fiero online service guide has a short write up on replacing door hinge pins at:<p>http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/osg/door-hinge-pins,html<p>I also seem to remember a write up in FOCOA magazine about replacing hinge pin bushings.  Call Phil Huff at FOCOA<p>(714) 903-6186  or write to <br>www.fieroowners.com<p>for the reference issue.<p>I have all the back issues and will be glad to look it up if you can find what issue it is in.<p>Hope this helps,<br>Carroll
